[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0f044b089133b4960169f9cba4f95c81918c106434ad3f85b9","text":"Implemented the minimal RP2040 breakout in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx).\n\nIt includes:\n- JLCPCB-imported `RP2040`, `AP2112K_3_3TRG1`, and `W25Q16JVSNIQ`\n- USB-C device port with CC pull-downs and USB D+/D- series resistors\n- 3.3 V regulator, flash, 12 MHz crystal footprint, boot/reset buttons\n- GPIO25 LED\n- side breakout headers and SWD header\n- no `routingDisabled` / `routing-disabled`\n- no `@tsci/*` registry component packages\n\nGenerated output:\n- PCB preview: [dist/index/pcb.png](/workspace/dist/index/pcb.png)\n- Circuit JSON: [dist/index/circuit.json](/workspace/dist/index/circuit.json)\n\nVerification run:\n- `bun run typecheck`: passed\n- `tsci check netlist index.circuit.tsx`: 0 errors, 0 warnings\n- `tsci check placement index.circuit.tsx`: DRC 0 errors, 0 warnings\n- `tsci build index.circuit.tsx --pcb-png`: exited 0 and generated outputs, but tscircuit still reported routing/pin-spec DRC messages such as missing trace reports and underspecified imported chip pins.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: USB-C aggregate selectors like `.VBUS`, `.DP`, `.DM`, `.GND`, `.SHLD` did not work; the connector exposed explicit labels like `VBUS1`, `VBUS2`, `DP1`, `DP2`, `DM1`, `DM2`, `GND1`, `GND2`, `SHELL1`...\n- Wasted most time: distinguishing real routing/placement problems from checker/tooling noise after `tsci build` still produced a routed PNG and exited 0 while saying “Build completed with errors.”\n- Helpful changes: documented built-in USB-C pin aliases, documented valid crystal footprints, clearer examples for custom footprints on primitives, and clearer mapping from build DRC messages to actual failed nets.\n- Friction points: `tsci import --jlcpcb` worked well, but generated parts lack pin attributes, causing pin-spec warnings. The schematic checker also emits a huge `VerboseSchematicNetLabel` issue that is hard to action.\n- CLI command that wasted time: `tsci check routing`. Passing a file gives “too many arguments,” but running it without a file throws `Not implemented`. It should either be removed from help, accept the same file argument pattern as other `check` commands, or provide a useful routing DRC implementation.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019df7b6-32b2-7820-a5da-1bcbe945e30d","turnId":"019df7b6-32c5-7fb3-9c6b-f139934fa7f9"}}
